From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:37:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] glm cuda: DFlash2 reads complete prompt taps at TP>1

With TF_GLM_PREFILL_REDUCE=split (the default) a split piece's glue posts only a rank's own rows of the residual
and shares normed, never x, so the tap after layers 5/14/24/33/42 read stale rows for every row another rank owns:
half of a prompt's drafter context at TP=2, two thirds at TP=3. Replies never change; draft acceptance does.

Each rank now taps its own rows of a split piece (tapPieces; .local copies the owners' rows in first), and
shareTaps hands the tap rows to every rank once the pass is done, through the relay that shares normed, at the
taps' width (5 x 4096). The glue stays split. A chunk that ends before the drafter's window (dflash.promptRun)
carries no taps, so a long prompt shares only its last window.

Upstream PR #1623 (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold/pull/1623), cherry picked from commit
4b0dac026451e6235d42eaad29d12b063f1e54f6 onto the recipe stack unchanged.
